<title>BELGIUM: EMU just a stepping stone - Belgian c.bank governor.</title>
<headline>EMU just a stepping stone - Belgian c.bank governor.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian National Bank Governor Alfons Verplaetse said on Thursday that European economic and monetary union (EMU) was a stepping stone to political integration and not a goal in itself.</p>
<p>&quot;Monetary union is a very important step, a challenge without precedent, but - and it may surprise you to hear this from a (central bank) governor - it's not a goal as such,&quot; Verplaetse told a Flanders Technology foundation lunch.</p>
<p>Verplaetse said EMU would herald greater European integration, gradually including all forms of taxation.</p>
<p>&quot;Eventually we'll arrive at political integraton, which is the main goal of the whole monetary union,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom</p>
